  "scientific_limits": {
    "en": "{\"representation\":\"living-reconstruction\",\"scope\":\"Whole living bone-crushing dog with short domed skull, deep jaws and heavy forequarters.\",\"scientific_limits\":{\"en\":\"Original genus-level living reconstruction, not a fossil scan. F:AM61640 B.secundus supplies real cranial anatomy; published artist reconstruction supplies a comparative body silhouette, not complete fossil evidence. Fleshed length, shoulder height, ears, fur and color are inferred. B.parvus body-mass estimates from other specimens must not be described as measurements of F:AM61640.\",\"zh\":\"原属级完整活体复原，并非化石扫描。F:AM61640 B.secundus 为真实颅骨依据；论文作者复原只支持身体比较轮廓，不表示完整骨架实证。活体长、肩高、耳形、毛与颜色为推断；其他标本B.parvus体重估值不得称为该颅实测。\"},\"original_inventory_ordinal\":643,\"taxon\":\"Borophagus; cranial reference B. secundus\",\"classification\":\"Canidae, Borophaginae, Carnivora, Mammalia\",\"scale\":{\"unit\":\"meter\",\"skull_reference_m\":0.21,\"skull_reference_status\":\"Approximate image estimate: side panel A spans about 6.9 times its 3cm scale bar. Not published caliper measurement.\",\"fleshed_head_model_m\":0.24,\"nose_rump_model_m\":1.1,\"shoulder_model_m\":0.65,\"tail_model_m\":0.36,\"body_scale_status\":\"Model proportional estimates, not specimen measurement. NPS small-wolf comparison and published reconstruction guide size; no exact live body dimensions established.\"},\"diagnostic_targets\":[\"Strongly vaulted forehead steps down onto shortened broad muzzle; not long narrow modern wolf snout.\",\"Deep robust lower jaw and wide cheek/zygomatic mass; small ears remain distinct above head.\",\"Broad muscular neck and forequarters, deep front chest tapering toward abdomen; not skinny fox or rectangular bear.\",\"Canid digitigrade legs with visible elbow/hock transitions and four weight-bearing toes, small fore dewclaw optional as inference; no hooves or feline retractile claws.\",\"Long moderate tapered furry tail; no hyena extreme spine slope, huge mane or obligatory spots.\",\"Closed or minimally parted mouth; if teeth exposed, no saber fangs, large posterior crushing teeth rather than identical pickets.\"]}",
    "zh": "原创低多边形研究；形态、尺度及不确定性严格以本次已核参考为界。原始限定：{\"representation\":\"living-reconstruction\",\"scope\":\"Whole living bone-crushing dog with short domed skull, deep jaws and heavy forequarters.\",\"scientific_limits\":{\"en\":\"Original genus-level living reconstruction, not a fossil scan. F:AM61640 B.secundus supplies real cranial anatomy; published artist reconstruction supplies a comparative body silhouette, not complete fossil evidence. Fleshed length, shoulder height, ears, fur and color are inferred. B.parvus body-mass estimates from other specimens must not be described as measurements of F:AM61640.\",\"zh\":\"原属级完整活体复原，并非化石扫描。F:AM61640 B.secundus 为真实颅骨依据；论文作者复原只支持身体比较轮廓，不表示完整骨架实证。活体长、肩高、耳形、毛与颜色为推断；其他标本B.parvus体重估值不得称为该颅实测。\"},\"original_inventory_ordinal\":643,\"taxon\":\"Borophagus; cranial reference B. secundus\",\"classification\":\"Canidae, Borophaginae, Carnivora, Mammalia\",\"scale\":{\"unit\":\"meter\",\"skull_reference_m\":0.21,\"skull_reference_status\":\"Approximate image estimate: side panel A spans about 6.9 times its 3cm scale bar. Not published caliper measurement.\",\"fleshed_head_model_m\":0.24,\"nose_rump_model_m\":1.1,\"shoulder_model_m\":0.65,\"tail_model_m\":0.36,\"body_scale_status\":\"Model proportional estimates, not specimen measurement. NPS small-wolf comparison and published reconstruction guide size; no exact live body dimensions established.\"},\"diagnostic_targets\":[\"Strongly vaulted forehead steps down onto shortened broad muzzle; not long narrow modern wolf snout.\",\"Deep robust lower jaw and wide cheek/zygomatic mass; small ears remain distinct above head.\",\"Broad muscular neck and forequarters, deep front chest tapering toward abdomen; not skinny fox or rectangular bear.\",\"Canid digitigrade legs with visible elbow/hock transitions and four weight-bearing toes, small fore dewclaw optional as inference; no hooves or feline retractile claws.\",\"Long moderate tapered furry tail; no hyena extreme spine slope, huge mane or obligatory spots.\",\"Closed or minimally parted mouth; if teeth exposed, no saber fangs, large posterior crushing teeth rather than identical pickets.\"]}"
  },
